WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Fatigue is a performance constraint.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.060
It can reduce attention, slow reactions, weaken working memory,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.000
and make error detection less reliable.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
In technical work, that might mean missing a subtle configuration problem.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
In operations, it might mean skipping a check.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.620
In writing,

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.935
it might mean failing to notice that the argument no longer supports the conclusion.

00:00:15.935 --> 00:00:19.200
Fatigue can also affect emotional regulation and confidence.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.000
People may become more reactive, more impatient,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.995
or more certain than the evidence supports.

00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:27.730
Overconfidence under fatigue is especially risky because the person may not realize

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:29.000
performance has degraded.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.800
They may continue making decisions with the same level of confidence while using weaker

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.245
attention and judgment.

00:00:34.245 --> 00:00:37.950
Performance risk matters in driving, safety-sensitive roles, incident response,

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.980
medical and operational settings, and any work where errors can compound.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.060
This course does not provide safety policy or medical guidance,

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.985
but it does emphasize that recovery is part of responsible performance design.

00:00:47.985 --> 00:00:51.000
Teams should recognize when performance problems may be recovery problems.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.902
Persistent sleep, health, or safety concerns belong with qualified help.

00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:56.430
In learning and workplace design,

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.935
the practical response is to treat fatigue as information.

00:00:58.935 --> 00:01:03.995
Adjust the task, add review, slow down when stakes are high, rotate roles when possible,

00:01:03.995 --> 00:01:04.985
or reschedule demanding work.

00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:08.870
Trying harder is not always the right answer when the system is under-recovered.
